      "0": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "HUB\n\nThe Hub node (also known as a Null in other languages) simply functions as an extension cord to tidy up your patch. What comes in comes out the same.\n\nIn this example we've used the Hub nodes to make sure that the wire from the Sine to the Circle node doesn't pass through the comment node. There is nothing wrong with passing through a comment node (they kinda like it), but we like to keep things nice, clean and PG13."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 195.2468414306641,
          "width": 661.3009033203125,
